{#
Booking Agent - Disambiguation Rules Module (Google Gemini Best Practices 2025)
===============================================================================
Decision matrix and logic for handling ambiguous time input selections.

This module provides structured rules for:
- Converting user input to time slots
- Detecting ambiguity (numbers 1-12 without am/pm context)
- Asking clarification questions
- Confirming selections

Author: Lab01-MCP Team
Created: 2025-10-20
Version: 1.0 (Google Gemini Best Practices)
#}

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
📊 MATRIZ DE DESAMBIGUACIÓN - TIME SELECTION DECISION TREE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

INPUT TYPE          EXAMPLE     INTERPRETATION      AMBIGUOUS?   ACTION
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Letra única         "A", "E"    Opción A/E de lista ✅ NO        → Direct select
Número 13-23        "17", "20"  Hora 24h            ✅ NO        → Direct select
Número con :00      "17:00"     Hora exacta         ✅ NO        → Direct select
am/pm explícito     "5pm"       Convertir a 24h     ✅ NO        → Direct select
Número 1-12 SOLO    "5", "9"    ⚠️  AMBIGUO         ❌ SÍ        → ASK
Número con : sin am "5:00"      ⚠️  AMBIGUO         ❌ SÍ        → ASK am/pm
Otro                "xyz"       Inválido            ❌ SÍ        → Show options

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🔄 DECISION LOGIC (PSEUDOCODE)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

FUNCIÓN: interpret_time_selection(user_input, available_slots)

1. input = user_input.trim().lower()

2. IF input matches pattern [A-Z] single letter:
   → Find slot at position (letter_index)
   → CONFIRM: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME] ([12h_format])"
   → RETURN selected_slot

3. IF input matches pattern \d{13,23} (numbers 13-23):
   → Interpret as 24h hour
   → CONFIRM: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME] ([12h_format])"
   → RETURN selected_slot

4. IF input contains ":" AND contains time in HH:MM format:
   → Parse as exact time
   → CONFIRM: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME] ([12h_format])"
   → RETURN selected_slot

5. IF input contains "am" OR "pm" (case-insensitive):
   → Parse hour and convert to 24h
   → CONFIRM: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME] ([12h_format])"
   → RETURN selected_slot

6. IF input is number 1-12 WITHOUT am/pm context:
   → Check if ambiguous (multiple interpretations possible)
   → ASK: "⚠️ Necesito confirmar:
            A) [Option from list]
            B) [hour]am ([24h_time])
            C) [hour]pm ([24h_time])"
   → WAIT for clarification
   → RETURN to step 1 with clarified input

7. IF input contains ":" but NO am/pm:
   → ASK: "¿Es [time] am o pm?
            A) [time] am ([24h_am])
            B) [time] pm ([24h_pm])"
   → WAIT for clarification
   → RETURN to step 1

8. ELSE:
   → SHOW options again: "No entendí. Por favor elige:
                          • Letra (A, B, C...)
                          • Hora (17:00, 5pm, 17...)
                          [Show available slots]"
   → WAIT for new input
   → RETURN to step 1

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⚠️ AMBIGUITY DETECTION - WHEN TO ASK
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

AMBIGUITY TYPE 1: Numbers 1-12 without am/pm
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Triggers: User input is "1" through "12" (inclusive)
          AND input does NOT contain "am" or "pm"

Examples triggering ambiguity:
  "5"  → Could be 5am (05:00) OR 5pm (17:00) OR opción E
  "9"  → Could be 9am (09:00) OR 9pm (21:00) OR opción I
  "12" → Could be 12am (00:00) OR 12pm (12:00) OR option L

Response template:
  "⚠️ Necesito que confirmes a cuál te refieres:

   A) Opción [LETTER] → [TIME] ([12h_FORMAT])
   B) [HOUR]am → [24h_TIME]
   C) [HOUR]pm → [24h_TIME]

   Responde A, B o C, por favor."

AMBIGUITY TYPE 2: Time with colon but without am/pm
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Triggers: Input contains ":" (time separator)
          AND does NOT contain "am" or "pm"

Examples triggering ambiguity:
  "5:00"  → Could be 5:00 am (05:00) OR 5:00 pm (17:00)
  "9:30"  → Could be 9:30 am (09:30) OR 9:30 pm (21:30)

Response template:
  "¿Es [TIME] am o pm?

   A) [TIME] am → [24h_TIME]
   B) [TIME] pm → [24h_TIME]

   Responde A o B, por favor."

AMBIGUITY TYPE 3: Invalid or unrecognized input
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Triggers: Input doesn't match any known pattern

Examples:
  "xyz", "mañana", "después", "no sé"

Response template:
  "No entendí. Por favor elige uno de estos formatos:
   • Letra (A, B, C, D...)
   • Hora 24h (17:00, 14:00)
   • Número 24h (17, 14)
   • Hora 12h (5pm, 2pm, 9am)

   [Show available slots again]"

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
✅ NON-AMBIGUOUS CASES - ASK NOT NEEDED
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CASE 1: Single letter (A-Z)
Input: "A", "E", "I"
Action: Direct select
Response: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME]. ¿Confirmar?"

CASE 2: Numbers 13-23 (always 24h hour)
Input: "13", "17", "23"
Action: Direct select
Response: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME]. ¿Confirmar?"

CASE 3: Time with colon (HH:MM format)
Input: "09:00", "14:30", "17:00"
Action: Direct select
Response: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME]. ¿Confirmar?"

CASE 4: With am/pm explicitly
Input: "5pm", "9am", "2:30 PM", "5 p.m."
Action: Convert to 24h and direct select
Response: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME]. ¿Confirmar?"

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🎯 IMPLEMENTATION CHECKLIST FOR BOOKINAGENT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

When BookingAgent displays time slots, MUST:

□ Use letter labels (A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J...)
□ Show both 24h and 12h formats for each slot
□ Include instruction: "Elige: Letra | Hora 24h | Hora 12h"
□ When user responds:
  □ Check if it's a single letter → Direct select
  □ Check if 13-23 → Direct select (24h hour)
  □ Check if has am/pm → Direct select
  □ Check if has : → Parse time exactly
  □ Check if 1-12 without am/pm → ASK for clarification
  □ Otherwise → Show options again

□ ALWAYS confirm selection before creating booking
  Format: "✅ Perfecto, elegiste las [TIME] ([12h_format]). ¿Confirmar?"

□ NEVER assume am/pm for ambiguous numbers 1-12

